            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 5,
              "start": 5
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "According to Scott L. Nelson (Petitioner), according to Scott L. Nelson (Petitioner), the petitioner contends that the rule at issue is a policy rather than a substantive rule, citing the New York Court of Appeals' view that class actions were not necessary in this category."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Mr. Nelson",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "2268f733e3d0b10606e25cff8f86fb6f08c5964eda773abc33e5944c292c4123",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-2268f733e3d0-0002-0002"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 47,
              "start": 47
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "According to Mr. Nelson, the petitioner points to the \u201cunless\u201d clause in 901(b) and argues that New York courts have applied it to both state and federal statutes, allowing class actions under the Truth in Lending Act but not under the Telephone Consumer Protection Act."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Christopher Landau",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "2268f733e3d0b10606e25cff8f86fb6f08c5964eda773abc33e5944c292c4123",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-2268f733e3d0-0001-0002"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 24,
              "start": 24
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "According to Christopher Landau, the petitioner raises concerns that allowing recovery of state law penalties in federal court could distort forum choices, invoking the Erie doctrine."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Christopher Landau",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "2268f733e3d0b10606e25cff8f86fb6f08c5964eda773abc33e5944c292c4123",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-2268f733e3d0-0001-0003"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 38,
              "start": 38
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "The petitioner warns that class actions could lead to overenforcement."
      }
